# Repo-ROOT .dockerignore. Every service Dockerfile builds with the repo
# root as context (`docker build -f apps/<svc>/Dockerfile .`), and Docker
# only reads .dockerignore from the context root -- so the per-app ones
# Week 1 shipped were never applied. Without this file:
#   - local .env files (real keys) get baked into images
#   - in CI, the host's pnpm node_modules symlinks are COPY'd over the
#     container's own install, and every build uploads 100s of MB of context
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.git
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate*
